00:32:11.080 --> 00:32:14.470
And Carolyn invited me
to say something about

00:32:14.470 --> 00:32:17.880
why France has such a
substantial Jewish community

00:32:17.880 --> 00:32:19.493
after the war.

00:32:20.710 --> 00:32:23.460
It's now, those of you who follow closely

00:32:23.460 --> 00:32:27.250
the New York review books can
see the the back and forth

00:32:27.250 --> 00:32:29.830
between Robert Paxton and Jackson Mala

00:32:29.830 --> 00:32:31.603
over justice issue.

00:32:34.970 --> 00:32:38.710
Many Jews survive in France.

00:32:38.710 --> 00:32:41.848
And it's Jews in particular
who were deported,

00:32:41.848 --> 00:32:45.450
but still a large number of foreign Jews

00:32:45.450 --> 00:32:48.740
who've taken refuge in France,
in the interwar decades,

00:32:48.740 --> 00:32:51.410
they too survive as well.

00:32:51.410 --> 00:32:56.100
And in fact, it's they, even
more than the native born

00:32:56.100 --> 00:32:58.567
who will be active in
(speaking foreign language).

00:33:01.600 --> 00:33:03.930
Which was one of the first organizations

00:33:03.930 --> 00:33:07.970
that pushes a Jewish memory in the 1950s

00:33:07.970 --> 00:33:11.503
when there was supposedly silent.

00:33:12.550 --> 00:33:14.283
The reasons for Jewish survival,

00:33:15.133 --> 00:33:19.300
some of that has to do with geography.

00:33:19.300 --> 00:33:20.850
There were mountains.

00:33:20.850 --> 00:33:23.970
It helps to have mountains, the Alps.

00:33:23.970 --> 00:33:26.180
It helps to have remote
countryside as well.

00:33:26.180 --> 00:33:30.100
So what which is why Jews
survival is much less

00:33:30.100 --> 00:33:34.360
in small countries like
Belgium or the Netherlands

00:33:34.360 --> 00:33:35.730
for that matter.

00:33:35.730 --> 00:33:38.453
It also makes a difference
how hard the Nazis tried.

00:33:39.370 --> 00:33:42.560
And whether they have the forces on hand

00:33:42.560 --> 00:33:44.370
to execute their policy.

00:33:44.370 --> 00:33:46.400
And in the East, they tried hard

00:33:46.400 --> 00:33:49.303
and they had the Wehrmacht to help out.

00:33:50.200 --> 00:33:53.500
And this does not come to pass
in France to the same way,

00:33:53.500 --> 00:33:56.870
it's so the level of
murderousness is not the same.

00:33:56.870 --> 00:33:58.830
But I don't want to again say

00:33:59.703 --> 00:34:02.470
what similar the argument that he makes,

00:34:02.470 --> 00:34:05.390
which is that there were many people

00:34:05.390 --> 00:34:07.443
to help Jews themselves,

00:34:08.520 --> 00:34:10.950
and particular native
born who had resources

00:34:10.950 --> 00:34:15.503
and language skills, and could
protect their countrymen,

00:34:16.453 --> 00:34:17.840
fellow Jews.

00:34:17.840 --> 00:34:22.840
But also non-Jewish French people,

00:34:23.470 --> 00:34:28.070
peasants in particular who
welcomed hid Jews in their homes,

00:34:28.070 --> 00:34:31.560
but also religious institutions
like Protestant churches.

00:34:31.560 --> 00:34:34.580
And some of you well have
heard of (indistinct),

00:34:34.580 --> 00:34:36.970
which was a Protestant town,

00:34:36.970 --> 00:34:39.910
which was ineffective Vilas refuge,

00:34:39.910 --> 00:34:41.610
a place where Jews could go hide

00:34:41.610 --> 00:34:44.050
in fairly significant numbers.

00:34:44.050 --> 00:34:46.110
But the Catholic church as well

00:34:46.110 --> 00:34:49.990
organized networks of rescue.

00:34:49.990 --> 00:34:50.823
And in fact,

00:34:50.823 --> 00:34:54.030
I've mentioned Saul Friedlaender
and he was protected

00:34:54.030 --> 00:34:56.700
and all cachet is called a hidden child

00:34:56.700 --> 00:34:59.990
in a Catholic school.

00:34:59.990 --> 00:35:02.050
And there are many
other instances of that,

00:35:02.050 --> 00:35:05.640
I could go on, but I probably shouldn't.

00:35:05.640 --> 00:35:08.810
Yeah, maybe I undersold my
book Carolyn a little bit.

00:35:08.810 --> 00:35:09.720
Okay.

00:35:09.720 --> 00:35:13.283
I appreciate your doing that.

00:35:14.890 --> 00:35:18.180
And then last of all there is
the issue of oppressed memory.

00:35:18.180 --> 00:35:20.580
And that's a tricky one, and I'm not sure

00:35:21.463 --> 00:35:25.950
that I negotiated it once
again, false modesty on my part,

00:35:25.950 --> 00:35:28.800
I negotiated it fully successfully

00:35:28.800 --> 00:35:32.510
because there is the puzzle
that if there a lot going on,

00:35:32.510 --> 00:35:34.720
why do people talk about repressed memory

00:35:36.210 --> 00:35:38.060
and with conviction.

00:35:38.060 --> 00:35:40.010
And I guess i say a
number of things to that,

00:35:40.010 --> 00:35:43.410
one is that when it comes
to internal life of families

00:35:43.410 --> 00:35:46.653
and individuals, there's
plenty of repressed memories.

00:35:48.143 --> 00:35:50.560
And so it's just in the public domain

00:35:50.560 --> 00:35:53.933
where there are narratives
being annunciated.

00:35:55.470 --> 00:35:57.650
That's where there was not the silence,

00:35:57.650 --> 00:36:00.270
and maybe these public
stories aren't satisfying

00:36:01.517 --> 00:36:04.150
to individual people, and
they don't see themselves

00:36:04.150 --> 00:36:07.810
in these public stories
in one way or another.

00:36:07.810 --> 00:36:10.440
But also, I try to suggest

00:36:10.440 --> 00:36:14.070
that some of the earlier
stories emphasize religion,

00:36:14.070 --> 00:36:17.600
heroism, martyrdom, and
that for younger people,

00:36:17.600 --> 00:36:20.109
they're not interested
in this kind of thing.

00:36:20.109 --> 00:36:21.050
And these are not stories that resonate

00:36:21.050 --> 00:36:24.827
with them in any particular way.

00:36:26.370 --> 00:36:30.250
And in addition with
France in the mid 1960s,

00:36:30.250 --> 00:36:33.870
De Gaulle is back in power and
he is putting the full weight

00:36:33.870 --> 00:36:37.340
of the state behind a certain
kind of memory politics

00:36:37.340 --> 00:36:41.430
for people who grow up in the
midst of that, in the 60s.

00:36:41.430 --> 00:36:45.490
It might seem as though
nothing else existed

00:36:45.490 --> 00:36:46.840
but De Gaulles's story.

00:36:46.840 --> 00:36:49.354
And maybe some communist story too

00:36:49.354 --> 00:36:51.750
if you grew up in a leftist household.

00:36:51.750 --> 00:36:55.990
And so at that conjuncture, in that world

00:36:55.990 --> 00:36:58.580
it might've seen that there was silence

00:36:58.580 --> 00:37:00.980
because other stories were being blurred

00:37:00.980 --> 00:37:02.990
so loudly in nature.

00:37:02.990 --> 00:37:04.440
And then last of all,

00:37:04.440 --> 00:37:06.990
the return of the repressed paradigm

00:37:06.990 --> 00:37:09.940
is one that begins to circulate

00:37:09.940 --> 00:37:11.540
in the 60s and 70s.

00:37:11.540 --> 00:37:13.990
And it's one that's
embraced by young people,

00:37:13.990 --> 00:37:15.820
that's why we didn't know about it.

00:37:15.820 --> 00:37:17.650
It was repression.

00:37:17.650 --> 00:37:21.930
This is how psyche works, this
is how national psyches work

00:37:21.930 --> 00:37:23.670
at the same time.

00:37:23.670 --> 00:37:25.910
And so that's the kind of explanation,

00:37:25.910 --> 00:37:28.433
explanatory framework that I explored.

